          },
          "properties": {
            "security-severity": "7.5",
            "strix_vuln_class_hash": "e8890f63629e080597eba549ac9b455739b0fda17f33a673a29ba50c64e4119a",
            "synthetic_location": true,
            "strix": {
              "id": "vuln-0005",
              "severity": "high",
              "cvss": 7.5,
              "timestamp": "2026-08-25 06:18:10 UTC",
              "target": "/workspace/CareCliQV2",
              "cve": "CVE-2025-71329",
              "impact": "An attacker who can supply crafted image files to the application can trigger a permanent denial of service by causing the Node.js event loop to hang in an infinite loop. This affects the **React Native mobile application** build process via the Metro bundler, which uses `image-size` as a transitive dependency. While this primarily impacts the build/development pipeline rather than production runtime, it can block mobile app builds and updates.",
              "remediation_steps": "Upgrade the `metro` dependency chain to a version that resolves `image-size` to **2.0.3 or later** (when available) which includes the fix for the infinite loop vulnerability. Monitor the upstream issue at `github.com/image-size/image-size/pull/439` for patch availability. As a workaround, validate and sanitize image files before processing during builds.",
              "dependency_metadata": {
                "package_name": "image-size",
                "installed_version": "1.2.1",
                "package_ecosystem": "npm",
                "manifest_path": "pnpm-lock.yaml",
                "introduced_by": "metro@0.83.3",
                "dependency_path": "metro@0.83.3 > image-size@1.2.1",
                "reachability": "imported",
                "reachability_evidence": "The `image-size` package is imported and used by Metro bundler (confirmed transitive dependency in `pnpm-lock.yaml`). Metro is the React Native build tool that processes image assets during the bundling phase. However, direct application code does not import `image-size` — it is used exclusively by the build toolchain. Static search confirmed no direct imports: `rg \"image-size|imageSize\" -t web -l` returned no results in application source code."
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "CVE-2025-71330",
          "ruleIndex": 3,
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "CVE-2025-71330 in image-size 1.2.1 (Denial of Service via crafted ICNS buffer)\n\nThe `image-size` package version **1.2.1** is vulnerable to **CVE-2025-71330**, a denial of service vulnerability affecting the ICNS (Apple Icon) parser. Attackers can permanently block the Node.js event loop by supplying a specially crafted ICNS image buffer containing valid magic bytes and a **zero-valued entry length field**, triggering an infinite loop as the offset never advances."
